{
  "name": "1942_velikie_luki",
  "title": "Battle of Velikiye Luki, Nov 1942 - Jan 1943",
  "notes": "Velikiye Luki, 24 Nov 1942 - 20 Jan 1943: 'the little Stalingrad'. The 3rd Shock Army (Galitsky, ~95,608 men, 743 guns, 46 Katyusha launchers, 390 tanks) cut off and besieged the 83. Infanterie-Division garrison (~7,000-7,500 men under Oberstleutnant Eduard Freiherr von Saß) in the rail-junction city; relief attempts from the west (Gruppe Wohler, 8. PzDiv, 6. Lw-Feld-Div, Unternehmen Totila) failed; the garrison surrendered 16 Jan 1943 (3,944 POWs, 113 guns, 97 mortars, 20 tanks/StuG captured). Rebuilt with full historical battalion names (en/de/ru Wikipedia + ru.wiki division pages + tankfront.ru). Attacker = the city assault groups: 5 GvSK north group (9 Gv/46 Gv/357 SD) launching from the NW strip across the Lovat valley marshes (9331 marsh: 2.5x infantry penalty, worse for vehicles, low cover) + 381/28 SD southern group from the SE (Toropets railway axis); 184 TB rides 30 Matilda III + T-60; 44 ski brigade; army artillery (270 aap) + 61 Gv.MP Katyusha ride line divisions (design rule: no pure-artillery divisions). Defender = the documented besieged garrison: GR 277 (I./II. bns), Pi.Btl. 183, Radfahr-Schwadron 183, AR 183 (I.-III.), II./AR 70, H.Art.Abt. 736, H.Flak-Abt. 286 (88mm), Werfer-Rgt. 3, Feldersatz-Btl. 183, 1. Sturmkompanie, garrison tank/StuG company (10-15 vehicles, designation unconfirmed). Excluded (not inside the city): III./GR 277 (dissolved by Nov 1942), Luftwaffen-Feld-Bataillone (no Lw-Feld-Btl in the garrison; the air force link was only the II. Lw-Feldkorps command), Festungs-Bataillone (term postdates the siege), 83. ID field elements outside the pocket, all relief formations (Gruppe Wohler, 8./11./12. PzDiv, 291./205./331. ID, 20. ID(mot), 6. Lw-Feld-Div, 3. Geb.Div Gruppe Klatt — the game has no mid-battle reinforcements). Org reflects historical strength: rested 357/381 (52-55), rebuilt guards divisions (50), worn 28 SD (45); garrison bns 25-40, StuG/Flak 40-45. Stats = 1942 calibration (T-34 armor 80 pierce 81, 88mm pierce 100, StuG III F pierce 92, Matilda III armor 70 pierce 55). Attacker: 73 battalions, Defender: 14 battalions + 2 HQs (synthesized one per division, DESIGN.md §6.13).",
